course: dictionary
lesson: 6488
title: The ending nd
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nd is not a word you say on its own. It is a short ending you write after a number to show its place in an order, so 2nd means the second one.
explain: Numbers that end in 2 take nd: 2nd, 22nd, 102nd. The exception is 12th, which takes th, not nd.
explain: Nd can also mean other things. ND is short for North Dakota, a state in the USA, and n.d. means «no date» in a list of books or sources.
fact: Nd is the ending for ordinal numbers that end in 2, such as 2nd, 22nd and 102nd.
fact: The exception is 12th. It is not 12nd.
fact: The letters nd also end words like «expand» and «comprehend», but there they are part of the word, not a number ending.
fact: ND (capital letters) is short for North Dakota.
fact: n.d. (with dots) means «no date» in a list of books or sources.
exercise: Sam came 2__ in the race. Which ending goes in the gap? | *nd | rd | th | st
exercise: Which is the correct way to write twelfth as a number? | 12st | 12nd | *12th | 12rd
exercise: Which is the correct way to write twenty-second as a number? | *22nd | 22st | 22rd | 22th
test: The library is on the 2__ floor. Which ending is right? | *nd | st | rd | th
test: Which is short for North Dakota, a state in the USA? | NY | NS | *ND | NB
exam: In a list of sources, what does n.d. mean? | new digital | *no date | north dakota | number data
